-- Stage 1 V2 migration draft skeleton.
--
-- This file is a non-executable design scaffold for Work Package 2.
-- It is intentionally stored outside src/main/resources/db/migration and
-- does not participate in Flyway discovery or schema history.
--
-- Before this draft can become the formal migration, every section below
-- must be replaced with verified MySQL 8.0.41 SQL and covered by the V2
-- migration static contract and isolated-database execution evidence.

-- ============================================================================
-- 0. Preconditions and migration boundary
-- ============================================================================
-- Input contract:
--   - Frozen V1 schema.
--   - sql/flyway/stage1/01_preflight_v2.sql has returned 25 PASS rows.
--   - No V2 columns, indexes, constraints, or relation tables exist yet.
--   - No production database or production credentials are used here.
--
-- This migration must not contain:
--   - CREATE DATABASE, USE, DEFINER, GRANT, or account management;
--   - foreign keys, triggers, procedures, or tenant-RBAC seed data;
--   - AI, vector, Redis, deployment, or unrelated business changes;
--   - DROP TABLE, TRUNCATE, or broad data deletion;
--   - IF EXISTS / IF NOT EXISTS clauses that conceal schema drift.

-- ============================================================================
-- 1. System-role transition protection and normalization
-- ============================================================================
-- 1.1 Add a temporary transition check that allows exactly:
--     user, admin, USER, SYSTEM_ADMIN
--     Use BINARY comparisons so utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci cannot hide case errors.
--
-- 1.2 Normalize only the two legacy values:
--     user  -> USER
--     admin -> SYSTEM_ADMIN
--     Unknown values must remain unmodified and cause the migration to fail.
--
-- 1.3 Change the column default to USER.
--
-- 1.4 Remove the transition check and add the final check allowing exactly:
--     USER, SYSTEM_ADMIN

-- ============================================================================
-- 2. Task identity and current assignment columns
-- ============================================================================
-- 2.1 Rename the sole V1 assignee column:
--     assignee_id -> assignee_user_id
--     Do not create a second assignee column.
--
-- 2.2 Add nullable columns:
--     assigned_by_user_id BIGINT NULL
--     assigned_at         DATETIME NULL
--
-- 2.3 Remove idx_task_assignee_id.
--
-- 2.4 Add:
--     idx_task_assignee_status
--       (assignee_user_id, is_delete, status, due_date)
--     idx_task_project_assignee
--       (project_id, assignee_user_id, is_delete)

-- ============================================================================
-- 3. Deterministic task backfill
-- ============================================================================
-- Use the single frozen derivation rule for every task lifecycle:
--     finalAssigneeUserId = COALESCE(assignee_user_id, user_id)
--
-- Backfill exactly:
--     assignee_user_id    = COALESCE(assignee_user_id, user_id)
--     assigned_by_user_id = user_id
--     assigned_at         = create_time
--
-- Do not restrict this update to active tasks. Completed and logically
-- deleted tasks retain historical responsibility facts.

-- ============================================================================
-- 4. Immutable task-assignment history
-- ============================================================================
-- 4.1 Create task_assignment_log with:
--     id                      BIGINT NOT NULL
--     task_id                 BIGINT NOT NULL
--     from_assignee_user_id   BIGINT NULL
--     to_assignee_user_id     BIGINT NULL
--     assigned_by_user_id     BIGINT NOT NULL
--     action                  VARCHAR(32) NOT NULL
--     reason                  VARCHAR(200) NULL
--     create_time             DATETIME NOT NULL
--
-- 4.2 Add the exact action check:
--     INITIAL_ASSIGN, ASSIGN, REASSIGN, UNASSIGN,
--     MEMBER_LEFT, MEMBER_REMOVED
--
-- 4.3 Add indexes:
--     idx_assignment_log_task_time(task_id, create_time)
--     idx_assignment_log_to_user_time(to_assignee_user_id, create_time)
--     idx_assignment_log_actor_time(assigned_by_user_id, create_time)
--
-- 4.4 Write one INITIAL_ASSIGN row for every task whose final assignee is
--     non-null. The deterministic mapping is:
--     id                     = task.id
--     task_id                = task.id
--     from_assignee_user_id  = NULL
--     to_assignee_user_id    = task.assignee_user_id
--     assigned_by_user_id    = task.user_id
--     action                 = INITIAL_ASSIGN
--     reason                 = NULL
--     create_time            = task.create_time
--
--     The insert must be set-based and must not use AUTO_INCREMENT, NOW(),
--     CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, ROW_NUMBER(), or execution-order IDs.

-- ============================================================================
-- 5. Weekly-review visibility and stable associations
-- ============================================================================
-- 5.1 Add to weekly_review:
--     visibility_scope VARCHAR(16) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'PRIVATE'
--     team_id          BIGINT NULL
--     focus_project_id BIGINT NULL
--     shared_summary   TEXT NULL
--
-- 5.2 Add:
--     chk_weekly_review_visibility_scope
--       allowing exactly PRIVATE and TEAM, using BINARY comparison.
--
-- 5.3 Validate on MySQL 8.0.41 whether the full target invariant can be
--     expressed safely as a CHECK:
--     PRIVATE -> team_id IS NULL
--     TEAM    -> team_id IS NOT NULL and shared_summary is nonblank
--     If the expression is not supported, retain the enum check and record
--     the limitation; PR6 remains responsible for the application invariant.
--
-- 5.4 Add indexes:
--     idx_weekly_review_team_scope_time(team_id, visibility_scope, year, week_no)
--     idx_weekly_review_focus_project(focus_project_id)
--
-- 5.5 Create weekly_review_task with:
--     id, weekly_review_id, task_id, create_time
--     PRIMARY KEY(id)
--     UNIQUE(weekly_review_id, task_id)
--     INDEX(task_id, weekly_review_id)
--
--     Do not create links for existing reviews. All existing reviews remain
--     PRIVATE with NULL team_id, focus_project_id, and shared_summary.

-- ============================================================================
-- 6. Post-migration verification contract
-- ============================================================================
-- The executable post-verify will live separately at:
--     sql/flyway/stage1/02_post_verify_v2.sql
--
-- It must verify, at minimum:
--   - V1/V2 structure and indexes;
--   - canonical system roles and final constraints;
--   - task backfill completeness;
--   - one-to-one INITIAL_ASSIGN reconciliation using task IDs;
--   - all stored weekly reviews remaining PRIVATE and unlinked;
--   - expected fixture counts from v1_to_v2_expected.json.

-- ============================================================================
-- 7. Promotion checklist for the formal V2 migration
-- ============================================================================
-- [ ] Replace this .sql.draft with a verified .sql under db/migration.
-- [ ] Add FlywayV2MigrationStaticTest and update FlywayTestSupport.
-- [ ] Run isolated MySQL 8.0.41 empty-database migration.
-- [ ] Run isolated seeded V1 -> V2 migration.
-- [ ] Run post-verify and expected-JSON reconciliation.
-- [ ] Append the final V2 SHA-256 to published-migrations.sha256.
-- [ ] Record the Work Package 2 acceptance evidence.
-- [ ] Only then allow later work packages to modify CI or runtime code.
